\viewkind4\uc1\pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\qj\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. \cf0  All praise to Thee, my God this night,
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0  For all the blessings of the light!
\par  Keep me, O keep me, King of kings,
\par  Beneath Thy own almighty wings.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par  2. Forgive me, lord, for Thy dear son
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0\qj The ill that I this day have done,
\par That with the world, myself, and Thee,
\par  I, ere I sleep, at peace may be.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par  3.  Teach me to live, that I may dread
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0 The grave as little as my bed;
\par Teach me to die, that so I may
\par  Rise glorious at the awful day.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li270\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4.  O may my soul on Thee repose,
\par \pard\li270\sl190\slmult0\qj And may sweet sleep mine eyelids close,
\par  Sleep that may me more vigorous make
\par To serve my God when I awake.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li270\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5.  When in the night I sleepless lie,
\par \pard\li270\sl190\slmult0\qj My soul with heavenly thoughts supply;
\par Let no ill dreams disturb my rest,
\par No powers of darkness me molest.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li270\sl190\slmult0\qj\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 6\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 6.  Praise God, from whom all blessing flow;
\par \pard\li270\sl190\slmult0 Praise Him, all creatures here below;
\par Praise Him above, ye heavenly host;
\par \pard       Praise Father, Son, and Holy Ghost.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\f2\fs14 
\par }

